# Mozartbrunnen, St. Gilgen (1926): the young Mozart playing his violin on
# a limestone plinth (48x72, art-director round 1). Statue (rows 0..23):
# head 4x5, coat in verdigris t/T, face, hands, violin (under the chin,
# pointing right) and breeches in bronze o/O/l, the bow a 1 px l diagonal,
# k outline (the Taube sits on his head).
# Plinth x 16..31, rows 24..55 = exactly the upper two tiles of the 1-wide,
# 3-high solid plinth (D-038: its lit w cornice top is the collision top);
# the bottom tile (rows 56..71) is the basin row and stays the stone tile.
# Two 5x4 bronze birds, o beaks 2 px past the plinth, spout light s/w/t
# jets from the beaks into the basin -
# small, bright and light, never the dark hazard lake.
# idle: 2 frames, the jets' highlights and splashes move.
sprite = mozartbrunnen
size   = 48x72
origin = 24,72
anim   = idle frames=2 ticks=12 loop
